Use appropriate PostgreSQL numeric/decimal types for money. Avoid floating-point arithmetic for monetary calculations.

Use a database transaction when creating an order and its order items. Prevent duplicate order submissions with idempotency handling or an equivalent reliable mechanism.

UPI:
- Create a payment-provider abstraction.
- Until merchant credentials and provider configuration are available, display UPI as unavailable or explicitly in demo mode.
- Do not create fake payment confirmations.
- Do not mark an order as paid from a frontend button click.
- Once configured, verify payment status using authenticated server-side provider APIs or verified webhooks.
- Verify webhook signatures and make processing idempotent.
- Never store sensitive payment credentials in the frontend.

Cash on Delivery:
- Create the order after successful server validation.
- Set payment status to PENDING until the money is collected.
- Display the exact amount due.
- Allow authorized staff to record collection with an audit trail.

Do not claim that the application can accept real UPI payments until a real payment integration has been configured and tested.

